# A common-emitter amplifier: a 2N3904 turning a 10 mV signal into one more than sixty times larger,
# upside down.
#
# R1 and R2 divide the 12 V supply to hold the base at about 2 V, so about 1.4 mA flows through the
# transistor and its collector sits near 6.5 V, halfway up, with room to swing both ways. CIN passes
# the generator's signal to the base without upsetting that bias, and COUT passes the collector's swing
# to the load RL without its 6.5 V.
#
# The emitter's resistance sets the gain. RE2 holds the bias steady, and CE bypasses it, so the signal
# sees only RE1: the gain is about the collector's resistance, RC and RL in parallel, 2.8 kΩ, over RE1
# and the transistor's own 19 Ω at this current, about 68. The output falls as the input rises. RE1 is
# small beside that 19 Ω, which itself rises and falls with the current, so the bigger the signal the
# less faithfully it is copied; a larger RE1 trades gain for a cleaner copy.
#
# Click the generator to turn it up. Past about 50 mV the output's top flattens — the transistor
# cannot pass less than no current — and further on its bottom does too, as it saturates.

# It starts settled at its operating point, every capacitor already charged to its bias, so the swing
# is there from the first cycle; `r` restarts it that way and `s` does too, while switched on from
# empty it would take a few seconds of the window's time to find its feet.

speed 2m
start settled

gen       G1    2 5   2 10   sine 1k 10m
wire            2 5   5 5
capacitor CIN   5 5   7 5    1u
wire            7 5   12 5

battery   B1    28 0  28 10  12V
wire            8 0   28 0
wire            2 10  28 10
ground          2 10

resistor  R1    8 0   8 5    47k
resistor  R2    8 5   8 10   10k

resistor  RC    14 0  14 3   3.9k
npn       Q1    14 3  12 5   14 7   2N3904
resistor  RE1   14 7  14 8   22
resistor  RE2   14 8  14 10  1k
wire            14 8  17 8
capacitor CE    17 8  17 10  100u

wire            14 3  18 3
capacitor COUT  18 3  20 3   220n
wire            20 3  23 3
resistor  RL    23 3  23 10  10k

label     in    2 5
label     out   23 3
meter     IN    2 5   2 10
meter     OUT   23 3  23 10
